{"title":"Tetration","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Tetration is an operation used in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Googology\" title=\"Googology\">googology</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Why_Tetration?\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Why Tetration?</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Fundamentals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Fundamentals</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Explanation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Explanation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#What&#39;s_Next?\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">What's Next?</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\"Why_Tetration.3F\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Why_Tetration?\">Why Tetration?</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tetration&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Why Tetration?\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Googology\" title=\"Googology\">Googology</a> is the study of large finite numbers. Mathematicians sometimes need new operations to write these numbers down. Some numbers, you can write with exponentiation. For example, a million is written by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da9479fe5edddb5e4922b35208dfdb0adbfd399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> and a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Googol\" title=\"Googol\">googol</a> is written with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b145a3cb05f988e18ba66891eadff1a319f4fb91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{100}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> What about googolplex, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b728048c088864ceb072df6e131df6e9a0a2e974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{10^{100}}?$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"19\" /> It can still be written with exponentiation. Let's say we invented a new number that had the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f9920786e424cd30cbfe8eedd494e0b6ef1261.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10}}}}}}}}}.\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"42\" /> Whoa. I don't think you would want to write ten 10's every time!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Fundamentals\">Fundamentals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tetration&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Fundamentals\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We all know that multiplication is repeated addition. We learned that in elementary school. The definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c2122a2865941250dd203f77e7eedadbd5fb3603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+a+a+\\cdots+a+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"180\" height=\"12\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />'s.\n</p><p>We also know that exponentiation is repeated multiplication.\n</p><p>Have you ever wondered what was repeated exponentiation?\n</p><p>Yep, you guessed it. Tetration is repeated exponentiation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Explanation\">Explanation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tetration&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Explanation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff9ba161b45362a27e8ac172ff95632641e989a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10^{10}}}}}}}}}\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"41\" /> with tetration, you would write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f934617b1cf636a84bae103face3341cbf60e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\uparrow \\uparrow 10,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" /> because there are ten 10's. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fb32e8d72b973c2e61414a72ca5e4c80ae43dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\uparrow \\uparrow 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adceab7777a603ae689afcdbba3c1a5da28c687a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^3 = 27,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> (there are 2 three's) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1f335c58a18dfca46e3fce4d437ab3e5e48046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\uparrow \\uparrow 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> would equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/315631d276d4439d82a5ad88e07dea31fe5c5881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{27},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" /> which is a really big number (around 7 trillion)!\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"What.27s_Next.3F\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"What's_Next?\">What's Next?</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tetration&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: What&#39;s Next?\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Now, are you wondering what <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentation\" title=\"Pentation\">repeated tetration</a> is? Click on the link to find out!\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018111850\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 85/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2566/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16102:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018111850 and revision id 93023. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}